# notes-api (Daylight greenfield sample)

Built by the Daylight factory from prd.md.

A small HTTP service for personal notes. Node.js >= 24, no npm dependencies; TypeScript runs directly via type stripping.

## Run

    node src/server.ts        # listens on PORT (default 8080)
    npm test                  # node --test tests/

## Endpoints

- `POST /notes` with `{title, body}` -> 201 and the note with an `id`; empty title or invalid input -> 400
- `GET /notes` -> list of notes in creation order
- `GET /notes/:id` -> the note, or 404
- `GET /health` -> `{"status":"ok"}`

## Persistence

Notes are held in memory only. All notes are lost on restart of the service.

## Logging

One access-log line per request (method, path, status, duration). Request bodies are never logged.
